sys: its parts, and the messages between them
  studio lays the pieces out from a note, studio/frame: fm, ed on what
  fm's cursor is on, and a shell. fm says its row to cur, and fm -f and
  ed -f follow it, as a lens shows what is derived from it. Each piece
  draws through outline, whose views are the terminal, gio's window,
  and the page next. A right-click is the word: tmux hands it to p, p
  asks c what it names, and o opens it.
tmux            the bus: your keys, the word under a click, the shell
  → p           the word
sh              the verbs: a script each, run by name
  c             the pronoun: cur, what the last verb was about
  p             text to the address it names
    → c
    → o
  o             an address to its program, by kind
    → e
    → fm        a folder
  e             ed in a pane, at the line
    → ed        +line file
pieces          studio, and what it lays out from a note, a slot each
  studio        the frame: its slots, each reached by name
  lens          what is derived from the thing: diff, figure
    → outline   draw
  fm            moves between things; its row is cur
    → outline   draw
  ed            edits a thing; a save says c, -f follows cur instead
    → outline   draw
    → p         a right click's word
outline         the tree a view draws, in messages
  → lens        key
  → fm          key
  → ed          key
  view          the terminal: fm's layouts, and a figure
  window        gio, at the end of a pipe, a JSON line each way
  page          the browser; next
libraries       what the pieces share, beside outline
  state         a window's cur and lens: where, read, written whole
  tty           raw mode, keys and clicks, escapes, and a wake
  watch         when a file changes: how cur is followed
  figure        a note as parts and messages: this one
files           the tree: one outline, from the root to an item in a note
  config        cur, the lens and c's log, in ~/.config/sys
  notes         rule todo design
  medium        pages, and the shelf: a folder in the browser
